data/kev-index.json — affected package versions for KEV vulnerabilities
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
This file is the build-time join of the KEV catalogue above against OSV, holding
the affected npm and PyPI version ranges for those KEV CVEs that have an
ecosystem advisory. It is what lets ceproof say that a specific component
version is affected rather than only that its product has a known-exploited
vulnerability. See scripts/build-kev-index.ts.

Three upstream projects contribute, each under its own licence:

Source:     OSV.dev
Upstream:   https://osv.dev/
Licence:    Apache-2.0
Licence at: https://github.com/google/osv.dev/blob/master/LICENSE

    Advisory-to-package resolution performed via the OSV.dev API
    (google/osv.dev, Apache-2.0). Individual advisory records remain under
    their own databases’ licences, listed alongside.

Source:     GitHub Advisory Database
Upstream:   https://github.com/github/advisory-database
Licence:    CC-BY-4.0
Licence at: https://github.com/github/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE.md

    GitHub Advisory Database (github/advisory-database), licensed CC-BY-4.0.
    Modified: only the affected package names and version ranges for CVEs in
    the CISA KEV catalogue are retained; all other advisory content is
    omitted.

Source:     PyPA Advisory Database
Upstream:   https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database
Licence:    CC-BY-4.0
Licence at: https://github.com/pypa/advisory-database/blob/main/LICENSE

    PyPA Advisory Database (pypa/advisory-database), licensed CC-BY-4.0.
    Modified: only the affected package names and version ranges for CVEs in
    the CISA KEV catalogue are retained; all other advisory content is
    omitted.

CC-BY-4.0 requires attribution and an indication that the material was changed,
which is what the "Modified:" sentences above are. Each one is also written into
the `sources` block inside data/kev-index.json itself, so a generated artifact
can carry the attribution without a network call. Advisory summaries, details,
references, severity scores and enumerated version lists are not shipped.

The version ranges are the upstream advisory databases' record of what software
publishers have reported. They are not a warranty that any component is or is
not vulnerable, and the file covers only the npm and PyPI ecosystems.

